  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you use a spell slot to cast a Conjuration spell that summons a spirit whose stat block is in the spell's description, such as Summon Aberration, you can modify the spell to summon two creatures instead of one. Both are of the same kind, use the stat block and rules of the spell, and appear in different unoccupied spaces of your choice within the spell's range, but their Hit Point maximums and current Hit Points are halved. If you lose Concentration on the spell, both creatures disappear. Once you modify a spell this way, you must finish a Long Rest before you can do so again, but you can also restore your use of it by expending a level 5+ spell slot (no action required).</p>",
      "chat": ""
    },
